# Contributing to {{project_name}}

This is the per-change workflow. Local + CI gates are aligned, so a green
local check normally predicts a green CI run.

---

## One-time setup (fresh clone)

```bash
cd /path/to/{{project_name}}
make install        # creates venv if missing, installs deps
make install-hooks  # registers pre-commit + pre-push git hooks
```

`make install-hooks` is separate so `make install` is safe in non-git
tempdirs (CI runners, smoke tests). On a git-initialised clone, also run
`make install-hooks` once to wire up:

- **pre-commit** — runs `ruff check --fix` + `ruff format` on every commit.
  If ruff modifies a file, the commit fails; `git add` the fixes and re-commit.
- **pre-push** — runs the full `pytest` suite. Blocks pushes that would
  fail CI on the same suite.

Both hooks live in `.pre-commit-config.yaml` and are versioned, so other
clones get the same hooks after `make install-hooks`.

### Codex CLI (required for `make review-plan-by-codex`)

```bash
# Install (one-time; see https://developers.openai.com/codex):
brew install --cask codex     # or per the official docs

# Log in (one-time; opens browser):
codex login

# Verify:
command -v codex && codex --version
```

### Claude CLI (required for `make review-plan-by-claude`)

```bash
# Install (one-time):
npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code   # or per the official docs

# Log in:
claude login

# Verify:
command -v claude && claude --version
```

If either CLI is unavailable on a contributor's machine, the corresponding
`make review-plan-by-*` target exits cleanly with an install hint rather
than failing silently.
