### After your first push to GitHub (required for `claude[bot]` PR review)

The `.github/workflows/claude-review.yml` workflow needs an OAuth token to
post reviews as `claude[bot]`. Without this secret the workflow runs but
the action exits with an auth failure — no review is posted.

One-time setup, right after you create the GitHub repo and push:

1. **Install the Claude Code GitHub App** on your account (one-time per
   user, not per repo): https://github.com/apps/claude
2. **Generate the OAuth token locally** (one-time per user; opens browser):
   ```bash
   claude setup-token
   ```
3. **Copy the token** Claude prints, then add it as a repo secret:
   `Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret`
   - Name: `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`
   - Value: paste the token

**The same token works across multiple repos** — it's per-user, not
per-repo. If you already have it set on another repo, you can copy that
value directly. Generating a new token does NOT invalidate older ones;
they coexist until explicitly revoked.

Verify by opening any PR after this is set — `claude[bot]` should comment
within ~1 minute.
